---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Built by Woodley">
  <main class="page-shell about-page">
    <section class="about-layout">
      <header class="about-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">About · 02</p>
        <h1 class="page-heading">Useful systems. Stronger teams.</h1>
        <p class="page-subtitle vt-tagline">
          I’m a principal software engineer who enjoys turning ambiguity into
          momentum—through invention, sound engineering, and mentorship.
        </p>

        <div class="role-line" aria-label="Builder, mentor, father">
          <span>Builder</span>
          <span>Mentor</span>
          <span>Father</span>
        </div>

        <nav class="about-actions" aria-label="Elsewhere">
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mattwoodley"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="button button--primary"
          >LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="mailto:matt@builtbywoodley.ca" class="button">
            Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <div class="about-story">
        <article class="story-block">
          <p class="story-index">01 / At work</p>
          <h2>Leadership through the work.</h2>
          <p>
            I’ve excelled at the organizational IC leadership level in Big Tech,
            and thrive when inventing, designing, implementing, and mentoring.
            I care about technical quality, but also about clarity: helping a
            group understand what matters, why it matters, and how to move.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-block">
          <p class="story-index">02 / Away from the screen</p>
          <h2>Craft is a habit.</h2>
          <p>
            Outside of my career, I build with my hands—from home renovations to
            “fine” woodworking—and I’m always looking for the next skill to
            learn. Making physical things keeps my judgment practical and my
            appreciation for constraints sharp.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-block story-block--quiet">
          <p class="story-index">03 / What matters</p>
          <h2>Life sets the perspective.</h2>
          <p>
            Above all else, my two kids, my partner, and our dog come first.
            I’ve travelled the world, but my favourite place to be now is home
            with my family.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
